WEBVTT

00:00:59.796 --> 00:01:03.996
had the same great great great grandparent
as their romantic partner.

00:01:04.036 --> 00:01:05.276
So why was that?

00:01:05.276 --> 00:01:09.756
Well, marrying a cousin meant keeping
money and power within the family

00:01:09.756 --> 00:01:12.116
and maintaining your social relationships.

00:01:12.116 --> 00:01:13.996
It was also about proximity.

00:01:13.996 --> 00:01:16.276
If you weren't traveling far
in your young life,

00:01:16.316 --> 00:01:19.076
you're more likely to end up
with someone you already know,

00:01:19.116 --> 00:01:20.276
like a second cousin.

00:01:20.316 --> 00:01:23.636
But even with the onset of the railroad
and the industrial revolution,

00:01:23.676 --> 00:01:25.516
it still took another 50 years

00:01:25.516 --> 00:01:28.276
for cousin marriage to go
out of style in Western society.

00:01:28.276 --> 00:01:30.116
Mobility may have played a factor,